# fac.lam - 7! on the Categorical Abstract Machine (cam.asm).
#
#   ./run fac.lam                                ->  5040
#   python3 lam2cam.py fac.lam                   (shows the core term)
#   python3 camdis.py fac.lam                    (shows the compiled CAM code)
#
# The syntax of ../graph/fac.lam. lam2cam.py turns the definition into
# rec f.\n.M, a recursive function: the REC instruction builds a closure
# whose environment contains the closure itself. Numbers are 15-bit, so 7! is
# the largest factorial that fits.

fac n = if (= n 0) 1 (* n (fac (- n 1)));

fac 7
